      "text_raw": "At high frequencies, the situ-\nation is again somewhat\nmore complicated.\nThe dominant capaci-\ntances are added in the cir-\ncuit schematic. They are the\ncoupling capacitors between\nthe supply line and node 1,\nthe output of the input\nstage.\nCalculation of the\nPSRR shows however,\nSS\nthat this capacitor is not\nthat important. The PSRR\nSS\nis zero dB anyway. This\nmeans that any signal at the\nnegative supply reaches the output terminal unattenuated.\nThis clearly proves that single-ended opamps cannot be used for mixed-signal analog\nprocessing.\nWhat is the origin of this 0 dB?",
